{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet","id":1492792,"title":"Has anyone ever done a time-traveler game yet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-11T02:06:08-07:00","id":1492792,"title":"Has anyone ever done a time-traveler game yet?","content":"One thing I like abt CofD is all the cool fangames out there, from Faustian mages to superheroes to mad scientists to lost gods to immortals to Lovecraftian kaiju and many more, but has anyone ever tackled a game around time-travel, or is it just too headache-inducing to be gameable? <br /> I feel like it could be great for horror, I'm thinking of a mood revolving around deja-vu. What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T05:21:51-07:00","id":1492796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet#post1492792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I like abt CofD is all the cool fangames out there, from Faustian mages to superheroes to mad scientists to lost gods to immortals to Lovecraftian kaiju and many more, but has anyone ever tackled a game around time-travel, or is it just too headache-inducing to be gameable?<br /> I feel like it could be great for horror, I'm thinking of a mood revolving around deja-vu. What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy: The Cursed 2E has a few scenarios that are tantamount to time travel, if you <i>really </i>play with the disconnected nature of their memories. Such scenarios involve the Arisen somehow awakening in the time of Irem before the Rite of Return, or awakening in the far future where humans have attempted to colonize Mars; Arisen have the benefit that you do not need to run them as having memories aligned to linear time. They will also have companions and cultists, plus enemies old and new, wherever and whenever their Descent begins across the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23800-the-firebrand","name":"The Firebrand","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T06:35:04-07:00","id":1492799,"title":"","content":"Not really, but in my oWoD chronicles it has been my regular go-to excuse to handwave timeline dissonance between Ascension/Sorcerer's Crusade and Ars Magica that came before it: Awakened retconned the timeline into what it currently is through Time magic, Paradox issues leaving fragments parts of continuities that put the Lie to the world that is of the Technocracy and Traditions both.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T12:04:37-07:00","id":1492818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Firebrand</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492796#post1492796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mummy: The Cursed 2E has a few scenarios that are tantamount to time travel, if you <i>really </i>play with the disconnected nature of their memories. Such scenarios involve the Arisen somehow awakening in the time of Irem before the Rite of Return, or awakening in the far future where humans have attempted to colonize Mars; Arisen have the benefit that you do not need to run them as having memories aligned to linear time. They will also have companions and cultists, plus enemies old and new, wherever and whenever their Descent begins across the ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>While Mummy is definitely the forebearer for the subject now, there's a lot of games that either feature time travel as part of the powersets of monsters or a prominent feature of the setting. Mage inherently has time travel through the Time Arcanum(I think you only need to 3 dots to get engage with it), the newly released Kith &amp; Kin for Changeling introduces wide temporal displacement as a more regular feature, and while it's not a highly controllable factor, travelling forward and backwards in time is discussed as a reason to return to Arcadia, Hunter's implementation of Interstitial Spaces has always had connotations of time travel potential, Demon's signature city is <i>built</i> on time travel as a feature (and has had it crop up in some of the other settings, such as Istanbul), and Deviant's weird science keeps a foot in a door(a cut sidebar from the upcoming Clade Companion was all about how one form in particular was a great excuse for time travel). There's also implied spaces where it's engaged with, such as nods towards the Werewolf Lodges of the Clocktower and Tindalos respectively.<br /> <br /> Particularly in a post Dark Eras/Mummy 2E, a lot of games have either added (or had the benefit of hindsight retconning connotations to the effect) some way to engage with time travel as a story mechanic without utterly ripping apart a currently standing chronicle that might want to explore it. The bigger catch is whether or not a playgroup wants to engage with it-even with Mummy, that is pretty effectively the time-traveller splat, just as much care is put into establishing that you don't <i>have</i> to engage with the Timelessness of the Arisen as much as you absolutely can.<br /> <br /> I don't think, in terms of a <i>splat </i>splat, there's enough meat on the bones of time travel to warrant it, at least within the context of Chronicles interest-but if someone wanted to make a big grab bag of time-traveller facilitation for al lthe gamelines and wonky weird powers alongwith that, they might be able to get somewhere. The largest I would go with trying to make a Time Traveller Explicitly kind of template would be akin the the Minor/Merit Templates you find in Hurt Locker.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T13:40:50-07:00","id":1492828,"title":"","content":"While I made it before Mummy, I have wrote a few drafts for a time traveler fangame called Conjurer: the Shattering, which drew a lot of inspiration from things like Pandora Hearts, Donnie Darko and Stein's Gate. Currently thinking of folding it into a Mummy/Mage supplement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T15:00:05-07:00","id":1492838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492818#post1492818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage inherently has time travel through the Time Arcanum(I think you only need to 3 dots to get engage with it),</div> </div> </div> </div>Constant Presence (Time 2) gives you a chance to remain unchanged by other people time traveling<br /> <br /> Shifting Sands (Time 3) let's you go back a scene at most, but you do so bodily<br /> <br /> Corridors of Time (Time 5) allows you to go anywhere in your timeline you can establish Temporal Sympathy with, but only as a kind of &quot;possession&quot; of your past self and only for the spell's Duration. Actually a kind of neat way to become &quot;immortal&quot;; jump back to early childhood with Corridors at Indefinite, and relive your life with Mage powers. Whenever you reach the origin Time, just cancel the spell and recast. Exarchs might take issue with you tho, so the Seeking should still be a priority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-11T15:07:06-07:00","id":1492839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492838#post1492838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Constant Presence (Time 2) gives you a chance to remain unchanged by other people time traveling<br /> <br /> Shifting Sands (Time 3) let's you go back a scene at most, but you do so bodily<br /> <br /> Corridors of Time (Time 5) allows you to go anywhere in your timeline you can establish Temporal Sympathy with, but only as a kind of &quot;possession&quot; of your past self and only for the spell's Duration. Actually a kind of neat way to become &quot;immortal&quot;; jump back to early childhood with Corridors at Indefinite, and relive your life with Mage powers. Whenever you reach the origin Time, just cancel the spell and recast. Exarchs might take issue with you tho, so the Seeking should still be a priority.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the biggest catch to this bargain bin immortality is the classic problem of wizards, in that anyone can reasonably cancel it out.<br /> <br /> Immortality comes in many brands, and many are worth what you pay for them. The excesses of payment that make it worthwhile is the general reason Liches are a problem.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I don't have my PDF's with me on fact, but yeah-that's where the tools start to come into play, and it sets the point that time travellers are not terribly uncommon in Awakening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T09:03:23-07:00","id":1492887,"title":"","content":"Someone did a fan-splat about it, called Oracle: the Endbringers<br /> <br /> I don't know much about it beyond a quick glance at the pdf, but I thought it was worth mentioning.<br /> <br /> Check it out: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...gers-fan-splat</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26440,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","user":"moonwhisper","date":". 09-13-2022, 08:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26440-moonwhisper","name":"moonwhisper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T16:15:51-07:00","id":1492933,"title":"","content":"The ones that come to mind are Mummies, Mages and some God-Machine shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Some additional ones would be to go to a Lower Depth where time is absent, have the players procure some kind of temporal buffer or time bubble, then figure out how to exit it at the point of their choosing.<br /> <br /> A far more complex option is to use black holes. Should someone figure out how to survive them, then time travel is possible. If the would be traveler could survive its forces, then move through the distorted space, survive the bent laws of physics and navigate the wibbly wobbly timey wimey ball, then they could exit the &quot;labyrinth&quot; in a date of their choosing. Setting up the systems to make all of that work would probably require an entire chronicle. But unlocking true time travel is too much of a legendary feat not to warrant that. <br /> <br /> Then a followup chronicle could take some cues from Chrono Cross to make them realize that they made a mess on the cosmic tier and now they need to fix the fallout.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-12T22:45:22-07:00","id":1492954,"title":"","content":"Let's just assassinate the Prophet. If we eliminate the embodiment of Tyranical Time, then Time should be free to flow as it pleases, right? :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T00:08:42-07:00","id":1492960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492954#post1492954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just assassinate the Prophet. If we eliminate the embodiment of Tyranical Time, then Time should be free to flow as it pleases, right? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck with that. If there's an advantage to being a tyrant symbol in the metaphorical backyard of the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/748737-time-arcanum-in-2nd-edition?p=763292#post763292\">bloody fairies</a> problem, it's that you are your own bloody fairies problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T02:21:56-07:00","id":1492964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492828#post1492828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I made it before Mummy, I have wrote a few drafts for a time traveler fangame called Conjurer: the Shattering, which drew a lot of inspiration from things like Pandora Hearts, Donnie Darko and Stein's Gate. Currently thinking of folding it into a Mummy/Mage supplement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh! Do tell me more!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-13T11:02:14-07:00","id":1492998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cauthon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492954#post1492954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's just assassinate the Prophet. If we eliminate the embodiment of Tyranical Time, then Time should be free to flow as it pleases, right? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Suppose you miraculously figure out how to unify all its possibilities and defeat the symbol of tyranny infamous for its incredible ability to predict the future, would the cabal be ok with the existential dread that follows? The Prophet defines the Truth of &quot;Great people shape history, everyone else follows or they are crushed&quot;, that works for positive leaders too, both mortal and supernatural. Take it one step further, the player cabal lead the story because they have such greatness, what happens if the cosmic contract enforcing that is missing ?<br /> <br /> Furthermore, depending on the Ministry, agents of the Prophet may seem neutral or even helpful at first glance. They don't sweat the small details, they can give up something valuable now to gain something even more valuable 5, 10 or 100 years down the line. They think long term, they look at the big picture.<br /> <br /> They can give you what you want, setting you up to self destruct by blind hubris. They could simply be engineering the scenario to make a future star cabal defect to the Seers or unknowingly take care of a problem for them. Your time travel device might be a convenient Iron Seal taking the cabal exactly where they want, because their actions were already accounted for, the trap laid out as a Xanatos Gambit serving his own interest.<br /> <br /> The Prophet's machinations can be a lot more subtle and meticulous than the norm, similar to the Nemesis, the information war and layered intrigue are their greatest weapons. His Ministers are the ones that would arguably be running <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Adjustment_Bureau\" target=\"_blank\">the Adjustment Bureau</a> as a front, with a real objective of inducing false or ultimately detrimental choices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 09-16-2022, 03:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-18T12:33:49-07:00","id":1493266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1492792-has-anyone-ever-done-a-time-traveler-game-yet?p=1492964#post1492964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ooh! Do tell me more!</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1JxYRZTBzUvYq6RkFfKyrwc3fmQVjs3ugJRgpExi056A/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Here you go</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.